@startuml component-background-jobs
!include elvira.iuml
' =============================================================================
' What: one facade (JobFacade) is the only way in: the single REST resource
'       /api/v1/jobs, the MCP tools and the domain triggers apply specs and read
'       jobs through it; apps never get their own job endpoints, they plug in a
'       JobDefinition (the contract) and the core drives every job through the
'       same state machine. Dependencies point inwards: providers and adapters
'       depend on the domain contract, the domain depends on nothing.
' Kind: UML component diagram, specification level, proposal (IP-031 rev. 2).
'       Layers (clean architecture): interface adapters, application, domain,
'       infrastructure; providers live in their apps. Omitted: auth, telemetry.
' Source: EvilFlowersCatalog IP-031 rev. 2; apps/tasks (2026-11-14).
' =============================================================================

title Background jobs: one facade, one contract, one state machine (proposal rev. 2, 2026-11-14)

actor "Admin · elvira-portal" as admin
component "MCP client" as mcpc
component "Service worker\n(ocr, lcpencrypt, …)" as worker

package "interface adapters" as adapters {
  component "REST /api/v1/jobs\nGET · POST (apply) · PATCH\nPUT runs/{id}/report" as rest <<proposed>>
  component "MCP job tools\nlist · get · apply" as mcp <<proposed>>
  component "Celery event listener\ncelery_event_handler" as listener
  component "Publish hook\nbefore_task_publish" as hook
}

package "application" as application {
  component "JobFacade\napply · patch · get · list ·\nreport · observe" as facade <<proposed>> <<focus>>
  component "Reconciler\nreconcile(job) per state machine" as reconciler <<proposed>>
}

package "domain (no Django, no Celery)" as domain {
  component "Job state machine\ntransition(job, trigger)" as jobsm <<proposed>>
  component "Run state machine\napply(run, event)" as runsm <<proposed>>
  component "JobDefinition (Protocol)\nspec model · check · dispatch ·\nobserve · on_report · scope" as contract <<proposed>>
  component "Registry\nname → definition" as registry <<proposed>>
}

package "infrastructure" as infra {
  database "Job · JobRun · JobEvent\n(Django ORM repositories)" as repo <<proposed>>
  component "CeleryDispatcher\nsend_task · control.revoke" as dispatcher <<proposed>>
  component "Beat: reconcile tick ·\nsweep · prune" as beat <<proposed>>
}

component "Providers: apps/<app>/jobs.py ×23\nfiles.ocr · readium.encrypt · extraction.run\nmaintenance.* · core.* · assistant.* · notifications" as providers <<proposed>>

' ---- layout only ------------------------------------------------------------------
admin -[hidden]right- mcpc
mcpc -[hidden]right- worker
rest -[hidden]right- mcp
mcp -[hidden]right- listener
listener -[hidden]right- hook
jobsm -[hidden]down- runsm
registry -[hidden]down- contract
repo -[hidden]down- dispatcher
dispatcher -[hidden]down- beat
contract -[hidden]down- providers

' ---- in -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
admin -down-> rest : HTTPS
mcpc -down-> mcp : MCP
worker -down-> rest : report (service key)
rest -[$accent()]down-> facade : <b>apply(spec, desired)</b>
mcp -down-> facade : apply · get · list
listener -down-> facade : run event
hook -down-> facade : run published

' ---- application uses the domain --------------------------------------------------------
facade -[$accent()]down-> reconciler : <b>reconcile(job)</b>
reconciler -down-> jobsm : transition
facade -down-> runsm : apply event
reconciler -down-> registry : definition(kind)
registry -right-> contract : resolves

' ---- providers implement the contract (dependency inversion) ----------------------------
providers -up-> contract : implement
providers ..> facade : observe(subject) on a domain\nchange (EncryptedContent saved)

' ---- infrastructure behind ports --------------------------------------------------------
reconciler -[$accent()]-> dispatcher : <b>dispatch(run)</b>
facade -down-> repo : load · save
beat -up-> facade : reconcile due jobs

legend bottom left
  |= Notation |= Meaning |
  | solid box | exists in the catalog today |
  | dashed box, «proposed» | new or reshaped in IP-031 rev. 2 |
  | blue fill, «focus» | the component this figure is about |
  | solid arrow | uses / calls, labelled with the operation |
  | dashed arrow | notification (signal), not a call into the core's internals |
  | blue arrows | one apply: REST → facade → reconciler → dispatcher |
endlegend

caption Apps contribute jobs only by implementing JobDefinition; there are no per-app job endpoints. A client declares a spec and a desired state;\nthe reconciler compares them with the observed state and takes the one transition the state machine allows (dispatch, block, cancel).\nRuns are facts from the publish hook and Celery events; providers that own domain state (LCP) report it through observe(), so the facade\nlists every domain job, also ones nobody started through it. The domain package imports neither Django nor Celery.
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · EvilFlowersCatalog · docs/diagrams/component-background-jobs.puml
@enduml
